          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebras"} vertex operator algebras
          %p
            This arises naturally in the descriptions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFTs"} 2d CFTs
            such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 2d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            which patchwise on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
          %p
            If the degree-0 part of a sheaf of vertex operator algebras is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            of the base space, then one one may think of the whole sheaf as defining a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"}> horizontal categorification
            ” of a vertex operator algebra and hence one also speaks of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebroid"} vertex operator algebroid
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+de+Rham+complex"} chiral de Rham complex
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fyodor+Malikov"}> Fyodor Malikov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lagrangian approach to sheaves of vertex operator algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~esiprpr/esi1828.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Formalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            in terms of sheaves of vertex operator algebras is in
          %ul
            %li
              Pokman Cheung,
              %em The Witten genus and vertex algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0811.1418"}> arXiv:0811.1418
              )
